  "rationale": "Genome-wide CRISPRi (hCRISPRi-v2, 5 guides per TSS, 1,881 non-targeting) FACS screens in Jurkat cells carrying a GFP reporter with the native RORC 3' UTR RNA switch (WT) or the 77-GA mutant, sorted into top and bottom 25% of the GFP:mCherry ratio, two replicates each (Nat Methods 2024, SwitchSeeker). The GEO table has an unnamed guide column; prepare.R names it, derives the gene from the guide ID and shortens the self-describing column names. The paper's Fig. 6a compares high vs low bins across both reporter lines, so the primary analysis uses all eight libraries with ~ pool + bin, where pool (reporter x replicate) pairs the two bins sorted from one culture (3 residual df). Knockdown of NMD factors relieves the switch's repression and is enriched in the GFP-high bin. The second analysis is the bin x reporter interaction, coded as an indicator for the 77-GA high bin (ga77_high) so the design stays full rank (the paper's 'ratio of ratios', Fig. 6b), positive when knockdown raises the 77-GA reporter more than WT.",
